============================================================
🧠 1. CONCURRENCY FOUNDATION
============================================================

Concurrent Execution ka matlab:
Multiple transactions ek hi time pe run ho rahi hoti hain

Execution actually parallel nahi hota hamesha,
but DB interleaving karta hai operations ka

Example:

T1: Read A
T2: Read A
T1: Write A
T2: Write A

Is interleaving ki wajah se bugs aate hain


------------------------------------------------------------
⚠️ Concurrency Problems
------------------------------------------------------------

Lost Update:
Ek transaction dusre ka update overwrite kar deta hai

Dirty Read:
Uncommitted data read ho jata hai

Write Skew:
Different rows update karke constraint tod dete hain

Phantom:
New rows suddenly appear ho jaate hain


------------------------------------------------------------
⚖️ Tradeoff
------------------------------------------------------------

Serial Execution:
Slow but correct

Concurrent Execution:
Fast but risky

Goal:
Concurrency + Correctness


============================================================
🔥 2. TWO PHASE LOCKING (2PL) — CORE IDEA
============================================================

2PL ek locking protocol hai jo ensure karta hai:
Serializability + Safe concurrency

Har transaction locks use karta hai data access ke liye


------------------------------------------------------------
🔐 Lock ka concept
------------------------------------------------------------

Transaction jab bhi data read/write karega,
usko pehle lock lena padega

Data ko bina lock ke access nahi kar sakte


============================================================
⚙️ 3. TWO PHASES OF 2PL
============================================================

Phase 1: Growing Phase
Transaction sirf locks acquire kar sakta hai
Release nahi kar sakta

Example flow:
Lock A
Lock B
Lock C


------------------------------------------------------------

Phase 2: Shrinking Phase
Transaction sirf locks release kar sakta hai
New lock acquire nahi kar sakta

Example flow:
Unlock C
Unlock B
Unlock A


------------------------------------------------------------
🔥 Golden Rule
------------------------------------------------------------

Jab ek baar lock release kar diya,
uske baad new lock acquire nahi kar sakte


============================================================
🧠 4. WHY 2PL WORKS
============================================================

2PL ensure karta hai ki:
Transactions ka execution logically serializable ho

Matlab:
Final result aisa hoga jaise transactions ek ke baad ek chale ho

Isse:
Race conditions avoid hote hain
Conflicting operations control hote hain


============================================================
🔐 5. TYPES OF LOCKS
============================================================

Shared Lock (S):
Read ke liye use hota hai
Multiple transactions same data read kar sakte hain

Example:
T1 reads A
T2 reads A → allowed


------------------------------------------------------------

Exclusive Lock (X):
Write ke liye use hota hai
Sirf ek transaction access kar sakta hai

Example:
T1 writes A
T2 read/write nahi kar sakta


------------------------------------------------------------
🔄 Lock Compatibility
------------------------------------------------------------

Shared vs Shared → Allowed
Shared vs Exclusive → Not allowed
Exclusive vs Exclusive → Not allowed


============================================================
🔥 6. TYPES OF 2PL
============================================================

Basic 2PL:
Follows growing + shrinking phases
Locks early release ho sakte hain

Problem:
Cascading aborts possible


------------------------------------------------------------

Strict 2PL:
Exclusive locks commit ke baad release hote hain

Benefits:
Dirty read nahi hota
Cascading abort avoid hota hai


------------------------------------------------------------

Rigorous 2PL:
Saare locks (Shared + Exclusive)
commit ke baad release hote hain

Strongest consistency


============================================================
❌ 7. PROBLEMS IN 2PL
============================================================


------------------------------------------------------------
🚨 PROBLEM 1: DEADLOCK
------------------------------------------------------------

Situation:
2 transactions ek dusre ka wait kar rahe hain

Example:

T1:
Lock A
Wait for B

T2:
Lock B
Wait for A

Result:
Infinite wait → system stuck


------------------------------------------------------------
🧠 Real Life Analogy
------------------------------------------------------------

Person A ke paas chair hai
Person B ke paas table hai

A ko table chahiye
B ko chair chahiye

Dono wait karte rahenge


------------------------------------------------------------
🛠️ Solutions
------------------------------------------------------------

Deadlock Detection:
System wait-for graph banata hai
Cycle detect karke ek transaction kill karta hai

Deadlock Prevention:

Wait-Die:
Old transaction wait karega
Young transaction abort hoga

Wound-Wait:
Old transaction young ko abort karega
Young wait karega


============================================================
🚨 PROBLEM 2: CASCADING ABORTS
============================================================

Situation:
Ek transaction dusre ke uncommitted data pe depend karta hai

Example:

T1 writes A = 100 (not committed)
T2 reads A = 100

Agar T1 fail ho gaya:
T2 bhi rollback karna padega

Chain reaction ho jata hai


------------------------------------------------------------
🛠️ Solution
------------------------------------------------------------

Strict 2PL:
Locks commit ke baad release hote hain

Isse:
Dirty read nahi hota
Cascading abort eliminate ho jata hai


============================================================
🚨 PROBLEM 3: PHANTOM PROBLEM
============================================================

Situation:
Query condition based hoti hai

Example:
SELECT * WHERE age > 20

Dusra transaction new row insert kar deta hai

Result:
New row suddenly appear ho jata hai


------------------------------------------------------------
🧠 Issue
------------------------------------------------------------

2PL row-level locking karta hai
Condition ko lock nahi karta


============================================================
🛠️ 8. SOLUTION: PREDICATE LOCKS
============================================================

Predicate Lock ka matlab:
Condition ko lock karna instead of rows

Example:
age > 20

Ab:
Koi bhi transaction age > 20 insert nahi kar sakta


------------------------------------------------------------
⚠️ Problem
------------------------------------------------------------

Implement karna difficult hai
Performance heavy hai


============================================================
🛠️ 9. INDEX RANGE LOCKS (PRACTICAL APPROACH)
============================================================

Idea:
Condition ke jagah index range lock karo

Example:
age index hai

Lock range:
(20, ∞)

Ab:
Is range me koi insert nahi kar sakta


------------------------------------------------------------
🔥 Real Databases
------------------------------------------------------------

MySQL InnoDB:
Next-Key Locks use karta hai

PostgreSQL:
Range locking approach use karta hai


============================================================
🧠 10. CORE INSIGHTS
============================================================

Locks control access to data
2PL control karta hai kab locks lene aur chhodne hain

Concurrency ko safe banane ke liye:
Conflicts ko control karna padta hai

Agar DB conflict dekh nahi paata,
toh usse prevent bhi nahi kar sakta


============================================================
⚖️ 11. FINAL UNDERSTANDING
============================================================

2PL ek balance hai:

Correctness:
High (serializability)

Performance:
Moderate (locking overhead)

Problems:
Deadlock
Blocking
Phantom handling complexity


============================================================
🔥 12. INTERVIEW READY SUMMARY
============================================================

2PL ek locking protocol hai jo transactions ko
2 phases me divide karta hai:
Growing phase aur shrinking phase

Ye ensure karta hai serializable execution
but introduce karta hai deadlocks aur blocking

Strict 2PL cascading aborts solve karta hai
aur predicate/index range locks phantom problem handle karte hain

Goal:
Safe concurrency with controlled performance
